# Generated newsletter drafts: reviewed and sent by hand, not source.
# Anchored: a bare "drafts/" matches any directory of that name at any depth,
# which silently covered docs/agent/drafts too -- and made it impossible to
# keep a tracked examples/ folder underneath it.
#
# The contents are ignored; the LEDGER is not. .last-issue.json is the record
# of what has actually been sent, and it is the only file here that is state
# rather than output. Ignoring it meant every CI checkout began with no record
# at all: the "no issue in the last five days" guard could never fire there,
# and `draft:issue` would have re-offered the same twelve listings the
# following Monday. The first real send, on 8 November 2026, reported "Ledger
# unchanged" and committed nothing, which is how this was found.
#
# Written as /drafts/* rather than /drafts/ on purpose: git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the directory has to stay
# visible for the negation below to mean anything.
/drafts/*
!/drafts/.last-issue.json

# Generated article drafts. Same rule as /drafts at the root: these are the
# pipeline's output, reviewed by hand, not source. 498 of the 743 tracked files
# were these -- two thirds of the repository was machine-written markdown, and
# 427 of them cited arXiv, which the editorial policy excludes. Three are kept
# under examples/ so the pipeline's output shape is still visible.
docs/agent/drafts/*.md
!docs/agent/drafts/examples/
.env.local.bak-*
